{
  "stage": "extract",
  "item": "EhU32O7DkA4",
  "inputs_hash": "55ab1febd1ad83c347456272a82c49f7fbe9df2e3ccdd5052e6d9b387bb3233f",
  "output_hash": "469a272f6ab428d8d9e2f36a959c082f1de0b249d691fcbf3ef6f6ed528f9b94",
  "output": {
    "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
    "points": [
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p001",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Top-k sampling is a decoding strategy for large language models that is used along with temperature scaling.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@25",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@26",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@29",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@31",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@33",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@36"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p002",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "A naive decoding strategy selects the next token as the token with the largest probability score in the vocabulary.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@61",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@64",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@66",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@67",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@70",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@75"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p003",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Selecting the next token deterministically by the maximum probability can lead to poor outputs, motivating probabilistic sampling instead.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@90",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@92",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@104",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@106",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@109",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@125"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p004",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "To use probabilistic sampling, apply softmax to the logits to obtain probabilities and then sample the next token with a multinomial distribution instead of taking the maximum-probability token.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@133",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@139",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@142",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@146",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@150",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@155"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p005",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Multinomial sampling chooses the next token proportionally to its probability score, so lower-probability tokens can also sometimes be selected.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@167",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@169",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@172",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@175",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@177",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@206"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p006",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Probabilistic sampling enables more creativity in the language model output and helps control randomness.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@227",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@229",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@232",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@235"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p007",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Temperature scaling divides the logits by a temperature value before applying softmax.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@237",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@238",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@240",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@243"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p008",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Increasing the temperature makes the next-token distribution more uniform, while lowering the temperature makes the distribution sharper and favors one token more strongly.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@245",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@247",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@249",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@251",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@253",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@257",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@259"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p009",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "visual_ref",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "An animation is shown to illustrate that as temperature increases, the token distribution changes from sharp to more uniform.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@266",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@268",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@270",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@274",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@276",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@280"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p010",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "A downside of using only temperature scaling is that all tokens remain possible next tokens, including completely random or nonsensical ones.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@317",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@318",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@320",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@323",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@325",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@331"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p011",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Top-k sampling restricts the candidate next tokens to the top k most likely tokens and excludes all other tokens.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@341",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@343",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@345",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@347",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@353",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@364"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p012",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "In top-k sampling, before applying softmax, keep only the top k logits and replace all other logits with negative infinity.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@373",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@375",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@377",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@379",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@389",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@404"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p013",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Replacing non-top-k logits with negative infinity ensures that after softmax their probabilities become zero, so only the top-k tokens can be selected.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@404",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@407",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@409",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@411",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@414",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@421"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p014",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Top-k sampling removes tokens that do not make sense from consideration as the next token.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@423",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@425",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@427",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@432",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@436",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@443"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p015",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Higher temperature values produce more uniformly distributed next-token probabilities and therefore more diverse outputs.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@459",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@463",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@465",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@467",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@469",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@473"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p016",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Probabilistic sampling with temperature scaling can explore less likely but potentially more interesting and creative paths, but it can also produce grammatically incorrect or nonsensical outputs.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@480",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@482",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@485",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@486",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@488",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@491"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p017",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "In PyTorch, torch.topk applied to the next-token logits returns both the top k logit values and the indices where they occur.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@543",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@546",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@549",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@552",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@555",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@559",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@565",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@572"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p018",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "code",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The code uses torch.where to replace logits that are below the smallest top-k logit with negative infinity, then applies softmax so that only the top-k tokens retain nonzero probabilities that sum to one.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@611",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@614",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@617",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@622",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@624",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@627",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@637",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@650"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p019",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "To combine top-k sampling with temperature scaling and probabilistic sampling, first mask non-top-k logits with negative infinity, then divide the remaining logits by temperature, apply softmax, and finally sample from the multinomial distribution.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@666",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@672",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@676",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@682",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@684",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@690",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@704",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@713"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p020",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "When multinomial sampling is applied after top-k filtering and temperature scaling, the highest-probability surviving token is sampled most often, but other surviving tokens can also be sampled according to their probabilities.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@715",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@717",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@719",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@723",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@725",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@730",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@733"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p021",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The full decoding workflow is: obtain the logits from the language model, keep only the top-k logits, replace the others with negative infinity, divide by temperature, apply softmax, and sample from the multinomial distribution.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@742",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@745",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@749",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@754",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@762",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@765",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@774",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@779"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p022",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "This combined decoding strategy preserves some creativity through temperature scaling, prevents random tokens from being considered through top-k filtering, and makes token selection probabilistic rather than deterministic through multinomial sampling.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@787",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@793",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@797",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@801",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@804",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@807",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@809"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p023",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "code",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The lecturer begins writing a final generation function that combines temperature scaling and top-k sampling to predict the next token.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@813",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@815",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@817",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@819",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@863",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@866",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@868"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p024",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "code",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The final generation function takes the GPT model, the maximum number of new tokens, the context size, the temperature value, the top-k value, and an end-of-sample ID as inputs.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@868",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@872",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@875",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@879",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@883",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@885",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@889"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p025",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "code",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "In the final function, the logits are obtained from the GPT output and then top-k filtering is applied.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@895",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@899",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@901"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p026",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "In top-k sampling, only the top K values in the logit tensor are kept and all other logits are replaced with negative infinity.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@904",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@908",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@912",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@914",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@916",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@917"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p027",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "After applying top-k, if the temperature is greater than zero, the logits are scaled by temperature, passed through softmax, and then the next token ID is sampled from the resulting multinomial distribution.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@921",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@924",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@926",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@929",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@930",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@932",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@934",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@936",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@938",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@940",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@942",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@945",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@947",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@949",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@951"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p028",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "If the temperature is not specified, the next token is chosen by taking the token ID with the maximum probability instead of sampling.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@953",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@956",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@958",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@959",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@962",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@966",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@968",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@970",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@972",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@974"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p029",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "EOS stands for end of sequence.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@982",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@985",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@987",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@989"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p030",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "If an end-of-sequence token is encountered, generation can stop early; otherwise, each newly generated token ID is appended to the current IDs until the maximum number of new tokens is reached.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@985",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@987",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@989",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@993",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@997",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1000",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1003",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1007",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1010",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1013",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1016",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1018"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p031",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "visual_ref",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The generation flow shown is: start with the logit tensor, apply top-k sampling, scale with temperature, sample the next token from a multinomial distribution, or use argmax if temperature is not specified, and keep appending tokens until the new-token limit is reached.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1018",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1020",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1023",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1025",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1027",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1029",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1031",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1033",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1036",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1038",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1040",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1043",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1046",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1048"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p032",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "code",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The generate function being used implements this token-generation process.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1050",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1052",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1054",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1056"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p033",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "code",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "In the example, the lecturer uses the new generate function with the GPT model, the input token IDs for \"every effort moves you,\" a maximum of 15 new tokens, top-k set to 25, and temperature set to 1.4.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1085",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1087",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1089",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1091",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1094",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1096",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1099",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1100",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1103",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1106",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1110",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1113",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1114",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1117",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1120"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p034",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "A low temperature produces a sharper probability distribution, while a high temperature can produce nonsensical output.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1120",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1122",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1124",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1126",
