        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p037",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The lecturer says the new decoding strategy solves the earlier overfitting problem caused by deterministic prediction.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1149",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1153",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1155",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1156",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1158",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1160",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1162"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p038",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Directly repeating next tokens from the source text is described as a classic sign of overfitting.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1164",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1166",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1169",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1171",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1174",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1176",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1177"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p039",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The implemented decoding strategies are probabilistic, which helps avoid overfitting because the model does not simply memorize the passage when predicting the next words.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1177",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1179",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1181",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1183",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1187",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1190",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1192",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1193"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p040",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "analogy",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The lecturer relates this to ChatGPT, saying it gives new output rather than memorizing what was written because of decoding strategies such as top-k sampling and temperature scaling.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1195",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1197",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1199",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1201",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1203",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1205",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1207",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1209"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EhU32O7DkA4:p041",
        "video_id": "EhU32O7DkA4",
        "lecture": 30,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The words generated in the example were not present in the original text, which the lecturer uses as evidence that the model is generating new tokens rather than memorizing.",
        "line_ids": [
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1213",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1215",
          "EhU32O7DkA4@1218",
